  "id": "COMPOUND:20876 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "Shikoccidin is implicated in the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2). This complex is known to regulate gene expression by methylating histone H3 lysine 27, and its activity is targeted by various compounds, including (2S,9R,11S,13R,14S,15S,17S)-11,14,15-trihydroxy-4-methoxy-2,6,14,17-tetramethyl-10-oxatetracyclo[7.7.1.02,7.013,17]heptadec-4-ene-3,16-dione, which is a known inhibitor of EZH2. The same pathway is also targeted by (2S,4R)-4-Hydroxyglutamic Acid and a more complex compound that shares the same target. These findings suggest that Shikoccidin may act through a common mechanism involving the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is then directed toward FaDu. The evidence supports a potential role for Shikoccidin in modulating gene expression through this complex, with FaDu being a downstream target of the interaction. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex in the biological response to Shikoccidin, and the observed targeting of FaDu suggests a possible therapeutic or functional relevance in this context.",
